# Single-page app fallback.
#
# The build emits one index.html and no file at /scan, so a static host asked
# for /scan?url=example.com would 404 before any of our JavaScript runs.
# Clicking through the app is unaffected -- React Router handles those in the
# browser -- but a pasted link or a reload on /scan is exactly the case the
# route exists to serve, so the host has to be told to hand back index.html
# and let the client resolve the route.
#
# 200 rather than 301/302: the address bar must keep the path, or the router
# has nothing to read.
/*  /index.html  200
